    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "**Step 1: Prime Factorized the Expression**\n\nWe start by factoring out the greatest common factor (GCF) from the expression, which is $3x$. This gives us:\n\n\\[ 9x^2 + 3x = 3x \\left(\\frac{9x^2}{3x} + \\frac{3x}{3x}\\right) \\]\n\n**Step 2: Simplified the Expression**\n\nNow, we simplify the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n\\[ \\frac{9x^2}{3x} + \\frac{3x}{3x} = 3x + 1 \\]\n\nSo, the expression becomes:\n\n\\[ 9x^2 + 3x = 3x(3x + 1) \\]\n\n**Step 3: Final Answer**\n\nTherefore, the completely factored form of the expression is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{3x(3x + 1)} \\]",
